WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
A British firm sells
goods to an American buyer

2
00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:06.620
for 1 million dollars,
to be paid in 3 months.

3
00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.990
At today's exchange rate,
that's worth 800,000 pounds.

4
00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:14.470
But if the pound rises to 1.40 dollars,

5
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:20.170
the same sale is worth
just 714,286 pounds.

6
00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:23.210
Nobody knows where the
rate will be in 3 months.

7
00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:26.440
So how can the firm know
today what it will earn?

8
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.130
In this mission, you'll
see what a financial market

9
00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.450
can do for a firm like this one.

10
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.410
Then you'll use a graph lab:

11
00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:37.010
slide the exchange rate
and compare two exporters.

12
00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:39.630
Your mission: find out how a firm can take

13
00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.950
the guesswork out of a future payment.
